[00:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'What you\'re about to witness might be one of the biggest moments in modern web UI. Every few years, something comes along that completely changes what\'s possible, and this UI library is one of those moments. Take a second to appreciate what you\'re looking at.'

[00:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'This simply wasn\'t possible in the browser before. This is HTML rendered inside Canvas. I think we\'re witnessing the beginning of a new era for web UI. Before we dive into this library, I just want to tell you that there is a place'

[00:27] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'called Shipper Club where all these legendary builders are gathering. We have so many legends from the AI world, from the open-source world, from the UI world, and you can be part of this group as well.'

[00:41] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'I hope I\'ll see you there. And now let\'s see this crazy library. It is called Canvas UI, and this is the first ever HTML in Canvas component library. I had no clue that something like this is even possible to do in the browser. And the'

[00:54] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'thing is that it wasn\'t possible until now. The tech literally didn\'t exist. We\'ll talk more about HTML in Canvas later. Now, let\'s see these crazy components. There are only 24 components inside of'

[01:07] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Canvas UI, so let\'s check out all of them. First one is called Asciify. So when I move my mouse over this image, you can see those ASCII things happening. And I have to say that it feels really smooth. I can say that performance is really'

[01:24] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'good, and it\'s not affecting rendering at all, which is really cool for something like this. Usually these kind of effects affect your performance. It feels slow, but this one is so smooth. And also one more thing I want to tell you'

[01:40] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'about Canvas UI, it\'s already a trusted shadcn registry, so you can just add all these components using one shadcn command, which is really cool. So this is the first component. Let\'s move to the second one.'

